│   Message:                                                                                                                                     │
│     I fixed `Segment._split_cells` in `rich/segment.py` so that it resets its scan to the start when the initial position estimate already     │
│ overshoots the cut. The existing segment tests pass (52), and a randomized check over text containing wide, zero-width and combining           │
│ characters found no cases where the left piece exceeds the cut.                                                                                │
│                                                                                                                                                │
│     The cause: the starting index is estimated proportionally from character count, and with zero-width or combining characters after a wide   │
│ character that estimate can land past the cut point. The scan then picked the wrong split. I did not add a regression test for this case.      │
